`hydra.utils.instantiate()` no longer eagerly resolves the entire configuration
tree. Interpolations are now resolved as recursive traversal needs them.
OmegaConf containers passed through with `_recursive_=False` are copied and
detached without eager resolution. Applications that rely on eager resolution
must call `OmegaConf.resolve(config)` before `instantiate(config)`.
Interpolations that refer to ancestors outside a passed container must also be
resolved before the container is copied and detached. Copied containers retain
flags such as `readonly`.
